{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/72555-let-s-discuss-pendragon-s-house-rules-for-werewolf-the-forsaken","id":72555,"title":"Let's Discuss PenDragon's House Rules For Werewolf the Forsaken.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-15T05:28:43-08:00","id":72555,"title":"Let's Discuss PenDragon's House Rules For Werewolf the Forsaken.","content":"Hello, everyone. I've made this thread for anyone who wants to talk about PenDragon's house rules for Werewolf the Forsaken. You can read about them in the link -&gt; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/729-ocel","name":"ocel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T11:06:00-08:00","id":72715,"title":"","content":"I used to have some house rules here too , But they are not included in the new forums <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> PenDragon is doing a fine job and really likes what he does . I will search my notes and compare rules with PenDragon as soon as I am able to . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T11:20:34-08:00","id":72727,"title":"","content":"I'll be using them in an upcoming game, so I'll have some comments then,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T16:48:47-08:00","id":72877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/72555-let-s-discuss-pendragon-s-house-rules-for-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=72715#post72715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used to have some house rules here too , But they are not included in the new forums <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> PenDragon is doing a fine job and really likes what he does . I will search my notes and compare rules with PenDragon as soon as I am able to . <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, what rules did I miss? I thought I brought them all over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T09:33:31-08:00","id":73234,"title":"","content":"I've used his rules. They are awesome, to say the least. I especially love PenDragon's take on the Gauru form. So much better than what we got now, IMO. Heck, I hope the new Gauru from the Idigam Chronicles looks somewhat like this. That would make me happy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However, looking over the houserule doc, I think I may have found a typo. PenDragon says Speed is calculated as Size + Strength + Dexterity. Yet, the Dalu form only gets a +1 bonus to Speed. He should get a +2 to Speed because Dalu grants a +1 bonus to Strength and Size. Unless, of course, this was done on purpose. If so, feel free to ignore what I said about Dalu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T12:03:52-08:00","id":73289,"title":"","content":"I have an ongoing W:tF game using most of the rules and I concur with Rahuman, they are awesome. While I've always loved Forsaken a number of folks disliked our very first game after it had come out, at least in comparison to Apocalypse. Gauru was quite significantly weaker than Crinos, the gifts and rites a lot less interesting. The one thing they did enjoy was the theme. So I knew I had to find a way to spice things up. After some time I found Pendragon's house rules and implemented almost all of them and when we started up our current ongoing game, at first I heard grumbles but one, two stories in I heard cheers instead. Now several of my players (even the hard core D&amp;D lover) has named it their favorite RPG. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Your like the Zadmar of WoD PenDragon. (Savage Worlds reference) My games wouldn't be the same without your house rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","user":"Xaielao","date":". 02-16-2014, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T10:42:10-08:00","id":74372,"title":"","content":"Aww, guys. I'm blushing here.<br /> <br /> Seriously I'm really glad to see that all my hard work is seeing some use beyond my table. Now, since house rules are a perpetual work in progress let me ask: Are there any hacks that have turned out too cludgy or confusing to use effectively? Or aspects of the system that no longer mesh well after the alterations? I must confess that I haven't really had as much opportunity to see these changes in play as I'd like, so feedback from those who have is much appreciated.<br /> <br /> Notably I'm finding that the Death rage revision may be too harsh, though that may have more to do with my gaping dislike of Kuruth than anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/72555-let-s-discuss-pendragon-s-house-rules-for-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=73234#post73234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, looking over the houserule doc, I think I may have found a typo. PenDragon says Speed is calculated as Size + Strength + Dexterity. Yet, the Dalu form only gets a +1 bonus to Speed. He should get a +2 to Speed because Dalu grants a +1 bonus to Strength and Size. Unless, of course, this was done on purpose. If so, feel free to ignore what I said about Dalu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch. Changed. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T16:58:06-08:00","id":75958,"title":"","content":"Well, after going over the document again and taking some time to reflect on the game I ran, I can honestly say that I haven't run into any &quot;cludgy&quot; mechanics yet. It seems pretty well rounded and runs smooth for the most part. Now, as for your Kuruth revision, I'm actually quite fond of it. I personally think it isn't really all that harsh. The only thing I found that was a bit much was the possiblity of every packmate entering Death Rage if one went there himself. I didn't use it in my game mostly for the fear of everybody entering Kuruth and killing each other. It might not have been all that bad, but I wasn't willing to chance it.<br /> <br /> Also, I do have one question. If using GMC rules, does the Pack Rank allow for all members present to deal Agg to Spirits of two Ranks lower like it does for an individual Werewolf? Meaning as a pack, if the Pack Rank is higher than any of the individuals, do they all deal Agg? Just something I feel needs to be clarified for future referance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And now, a side note. I noticed that with GMC rules and Dalu dealing Lethal with it's claws, the Gift Crushing Blow has become almost completly useless. What do you think can be done to fix this? In my game, I made it so that Crushing Blow granted a +1 Lethal weapon bonus to all Brawl and Weaponary damage. Is this too much? What do you think if it's no trouble asking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T17:28:22-08:00","id":75976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/72555-let-s-discuss-pendragon-s-house-rules-for-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=75958#post75958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, after going over the document again and taking some time to reflect on the game I ran, I can honestly say that I haven't run into any &quot;cludgy&quot; mechanics yet. It seems pretty well rounded and runs smooth for the most part. Now, as for your Kuruth revision, I'm actually quite fond of it. I personally think it isn't really all that harsh. The only thing I found that was a bit much was the possiblity of every packmate entering Death Rage if one went there himself. I didn't use it in my game mostly for the fear of everybody entering Kuruth and killing each other. It might not have been all that bad, but I wasn't willing to chance it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in Death Rage a Werewolf will not turn on his pack-mates (Kuruth revision, Paragraph #2). But I can understand the concern.<br /> <br /> My current issue with Kuruth is that in my games Werewolf PC isn't remotely geared for combat, and Death Rage is more often a death sentence to herself rather than those around her. She's managed to survive the few times she has raged, but it was dicey<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/72555-let-s-discuss-pendragon-s-house-rules-for-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=75958#post75958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I do have one question. If using GMC rules, does the Pack Rank allow for all members present to deal Agg to Spirits of two Ranks lower like it does for an individual Werewolf? Meaning as a pack, if the Pack Rank is higher than any of the individuals, do they all deal Agg? Just something I feel needs to be clarified for future referance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeppers. Being attacked by a wolf pack sucks mightily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/72555-let-s-discuss-pendragon-s-house-rules-for-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=75958#post75958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now, a side note. I noticed that with GMC rules and Dalu dealing Lethal with it's claws, the Gift Crushing Blow has become almost completly useless. What do you think can be done to fix this? In my game, I made it so that Crushing Blow granted a +1 Lethal weapon bonus to all Brawl and Weaponary damage. Is this too much? What do you think if it's no trouble asking?</div> </div> </div> </div>How's this:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Crushing Blow \u2022</b><br /> Cost: 1 Essence (None in Gauru)<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> <br /> The Uratha's claws, teeth and fists surge with might, delivering devastating attacks. All his unarmed attacks deal lethal damage, as though he were armed with a +0 damage weapon, and he reduces by one the damage requirement to inflict Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack or similar Tilts. If he manifests claws or fangs they are strengthened as well, gaining Armor Piercing 1 and reducing the durability of struck objects by 1. Finally, he may activate this Gift for free any time he enters Gauru form, though it deactivates when he shifts down.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T18:15:27-08:00","id":76005,"title":"","content":"Wow, that version of Crushing Blow looks pretty good. Much better thought out than mine. I'll have to playtest it soon.<br /> <br /> Now, concerning your non-combat Werewolf player and Death Rage. Something I noticed about using GMC rules makes it very hard to be a terrifying Werewolf when you can't throw a punch or use your claws. One of my players had a very difficult time playing a non-combat Werewolf. He didn't help much with hunts and could not back up anyone in a fight. But man was he a great hacker. Anyway, my point is I don't think anythings wrong with your Death Rage revision or your non-combat Werewolf. It's just my observations shows Werewolves can't really afford to not be combatants with GMC rules. Those rules for now don't really complament Werewolves. Don't know if tha